<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A HashSet internally uses a HashMap to store its elements. When you add an element to a HashSet, it is first hashed using the hashCode\(\) method.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
452 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The hash code is then used to find the corresponding bucket in the HashMap. If the bucket is empty, the element is added to the bucket. If the bucket is not empty, the element is compared to the other elements in the bucket using the equals\(\) method. If the element is equal to any of the other elements in the bucket, it is not added to the HashSet.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
