/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Preemptive scheduling is when the operating system can forcibly remove a thread from the CPU and give it to another thread. Time-slicing is when each thread is given a certain amount of time to run on the CPU. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [31]
>>
endobj
541 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The main difference is that in preemptive scheduling, the operating system can interrupt a thread at any time, while in time-slicing, the thread is only interrupted when it has used up its allotted time.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [32]
>>
